  "findings": {
    "CCTV-4 official": {
      "currentHttpStatus": 403,
      "details": "Direct HTTP clients and native libmpv all receive 403 with multiple standard User-Agent values. Updating decoder settings does not authorize a denied source; upstream must supply a currently accepted URL."
    },
    "CCTV-4 overseas": {
      "details": "H.264/AAC decodes. Startup and progress latency varied significantly between runs, including about 6 to 28 seconds. Native network timeout increased from 5 to 15 seconds; HLS analysis budget is 1 second. This is not a missing codec.",
      "deviceLimit": "Android TV full-decoder auto and software paths failed this run. Reducing native stream-info probing allowed decoded H.264/AAC parameters, then the emulator GPU context failed during texture setup. Those experimental overrides are not shipped. Native fatal playback logs are now reported so the host can advance to another backend instead of waiting for a secondary seek warning."
    },
    "CCTV-6 resolver": {
      "details": "Lavf/default clients receive HTTP 423 after redirect. Mozilla/5.0 receives MP4 and decodes H.264/AAC at 1920x1080. However the ~16.8 second MP4 is an upstream server-overload notice, not the live CCTV-6 broadcast. The notice explicitly asks viewers to switch channels."
    },
    "TVBS": {
      "details": "The master has two 1080p streams at about 2.89 and 1.24 Mbps. Native master probing opens both variants; joining incomplete H.264 headers recovers once SPS/PPS arrive. The high bitrate branch still stalled in one retest. Selecting one safe muxed variant and lower bandwidth during recovery yielded decoded audio/video and clock advancement."
    }
  },
